<!DOCTYPE html>
<!-- Quantum HTML + CSS example 01_text_elements/04: Blockquote, q and cite -->
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Blockquote, q and cite</title>
  <style>
    *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
    body {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
      line-height: 1.5;
      color: #1f2933;
      background: #f5f7fa;
    }
    .demo { max-width: 60rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1.25rem; }
    .demo > h1 { margin: 0 0 0.25rem; font-size: 2rem; }
    .lead { margin: 0 0 2rem; color: #52606d; }

    .card { background: #fff; border-radius: 12px; padding: 1.5rem; box-shadow: 0 1px 3px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.12); }
    blockquote {
      margin: 1rem 0;
      padding: 0.75rem 1.25rem;
      border-left: 4px solid #3b82f6;
      background: #eff6ff;
      font-size: 1.15rem;
    }
    blockquote footer { margin-top: 0.5rem; font-size: 0.9rem; color: #52606d; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main class="demo">
    <h1>Blockquote, q and cite</h1>
    <p class="lead">Quoting other people properly.</p>
    <section class="card">
      <blockquote cite="https://www.w3.org/People/Berners-Lee/">
        <p>The Web does not just connect machines, it connects people.</p>
        <footer>&mdash; <cite>Tim Berners-Lee</cite></footer>
      </blockquote>
      <p>As the saying goes, <q>simple things should be simple</q>.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
